On Wed, 20 Mar 2002 20:59, Myers, Robert wrote:
> In your research into security enhancements and options for SELinux, has
> anyone come across a COTS packages providing external security management
> capabilities for Linux or Unix OSs?  We are presently evaluating a package

>From my experience commercial software to address enterprise needs seems to 
be of a very low quality.  There just isn't a competitive need to write good 
software as customers get locked in so easily.

I suggest that your best option in terms of getting a working product, 
minimising expenses, and getting support is to start an open source project 
based on the SE Linux work.  There are quite a number of companies who would 
be very interested in tendering for such work who would probably quote rates 
much lower than the license fees of COTS software.


Also if you want to seriously discuss various options in such areas then 
attending OLS would be a good idea.


Russell Coker

